## Interlude / Side B — English Translation (Chapters 31–35)

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 31 — From Settled Grief
################################################################################

translate en b31_005:
    "Pak Ageng walks over to an old wooden cabinet in the corner of the room. Not the glass cabinet with the red tapes — a private one, always kept locked. Its brass key is rusted. From inside, he pulls out a worn cassette with a yellowed label. The faded black ink reads: {i}Siti, 1994{/i}."

translate en b31_006:
    ageng "Back then, decades ago, I was a sound technician. At a local radio station, right here in this city. I loved that job. Still, I loved my wife way more. Her name was Siti."

translate en b31_007:
    ageng "Her laugh… man. Best laugh I ever heard. Even on the gloomiest day in Malang, the second she laughed, everything felt warm."

translate en b31_008:
    "Pak Ageng's eyes glisten, catching the reflection of the shop's yellow hanging lamp."

translate en b31_009:
    ageng "Then one day she was gone. Illness. So fast. I never even got the chance to properly record her voice on tape. Once she was gone, our house went quiet. Way too quiet. To the point where I almost— {i}(stopping, shaking his head slowly){/i} …yeah. That bad."

translate en b31_010:
    "He walks back behind the counter and sets the cassette labeled Siti down on the table in front of Kai."

translate en b31_011:
    ageng "After that, I got obsessed. I threw every bit of frequency engineering I knew at it. Modified recorder circuits. Hunted down the finest magnetic tape I could find. All for one crazy goal: I wanted to catch whatever lingering vibrations of Siti's voice were still floating out there in the world. Hear her voice one more time. Just once."

translate en b31_012:
    ageng "For years, Kai. Locked in a dark room. Filtering out noise. Boosting quiet frequencies. Trying to rewind time through sound waves."

translate en b31_013:
    ageng "Until one day a cruel truth hit me. A voice that's gone is never coming back whole. What got caught on this tape isn't Siti. {i}(tapping the cassette gently){/i} It's the echo of my own grief. Spinning on and on, never ending."

translate en b31_014:
    kai_hati "…"

translate en b31_015:
    ageng "I opened this shop because I wanted to build a space for people lost inside their own anxiety. I modified those tapes so they could pick up what's projecting inside a person's head — their deepest fear about tomorrow. Because fear is the strongest frequency our brains put out."

translate en b31_016:
    ageng "{i}(looking Kai straight in the eye){/i} At the end of the day, though, Kai, those tapes are just tools. What they record is your own anxiety. Not some fixed fate."

translate en b31r_001:
    "Gema Masa is quiet in a different way this afternoon. No future tapes spinning. No hum of anything at all. Just cold air slipping under the door, and black coffee on the counter going lukewarm. Pak Ageng is wiping down an old turntable — painfully slow, like every wipe weighs a ton."

translate en b31r_002:
    ageng "You know, Kai… Plenty of people think there's magic in this place. They come in here looking for miracles. Thinking I hold the key to unlock fate."

translate en b31r_003:
    "He sets the rag down. Stares blankly at the turntable."

translate en b31r_004:
    ageng "Truth is, this shop wasn't born out of magic. This shop was born out of grief."

translate en b31r_005:
    kai_hati "…Grief? Pak Ageng never talks about himself. Never."

translate en b31r_006:
    "Kai looks at Siti's tape on the counter. Then down at his own hand — gripping the red August 1st cassette."

translate en b31r_007:
    kai "{i}(softly, tears spilling over){/i} I sacrificed my past, Pak… because I was scared of facing grief in the future."

translate en b31r_008:
    ageng "{i}(resting a hand on Kai's shoulder){/i} And if you keep going down this road, kid, you're building the exact same grief I went through back then. Only difference is, you're making it yourself."

translate en b31r_009:
    ageng "Don't let this shop steal your life the way it stole the rest of mine. Fix your tape… while it hasn't snapped yet — durung."

translate en b31s_001:
    "That afternoon Kai didn't just come to buy a tape. The back shelves were a mess after Pak Ageng cleared them out earlier that morning, so Kai offered to help reorganize. Pak Ageng wipes down an old turntable in between sorting — painfully slow, like every wipe weighs a ton."

translate en b31s_002:
    kai "Pak, does this record player still work?"

translate en b31s_003:
    ageng "Sometimes it does, sometimes it doesn't. Just like its owner. {i}(pauses; sets the rag down){/i} You know, Kai… Plenty of people think there's magic in this place. They come looking for miracles. Thinking I hold the key to unlock fate. Truth is, this shop wasn't born out of magic. This shop was born out of grief."

translate en b31s_004:
    kai_hati "…Grief? Pak Ageng never talks about himself. Never."

translate en b31s_005:
    "The cassette labeled Siti now sits on the table, surrounded by half-sorted stacks of tapes. Kai stares at it for a long time. His hands are empty — there's no red tape in his grip on this road. Still, Pak Ageng's words lodge themselves in his head in a whole different way."

translate en b31s_006:
    kai "Pak… if these tapes only record my own anxiety… then all this time, what I've been listening to every night was…"

translate en b31s_007:
    ageng "Your own voice, kid. Scared out of its mind. {i}(patting Kai's shoulder gently){/i} That's why I'm telling you: don't let this shop steal your life the way it stole the rest of mine. You still stop by a lot for the regular ones, right? Even those, if you keep leaning on them, end up the same."

translate en b31s_008:
    ageng "Fix your tape… while it hasn't snapped yet — durung."

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 32 — Good News in the Quiet
################################################################################

translate en b32_001:
    "That morning, before any announcements go up, Yara catches Kai in the hallway. In her hands is a folder with her portfolio — the school asked for one final copy for the archives, complete with an official title."

translate en b32_002:
    yara "Kai, hang on. Help me pick, please. I need to lock in one title for this final copy and I'm totally stuck. I like all three, just for totally different reasons."

translate en b32_003:
    kai "You're asking me? I'm just the guy who hauls the tripod."

translate en b32_004:
    yara "That's exactly why. You heard all the recordings back when they were completely raw. Come on, pick one. Whichever feels the most \"me\" to you."

translate en b32_005a:
    yara "{i}(smiling){/i} …Yeah. That really is what I've been chasing from the start. Okay. That one."

translate en b32_005b:
    yara "Hah, that's actually my favorite title. Malang sounds small, yet the sounds in it… {i}(nodding){/i} Okay, that one."

translate en b32_005c:
    yara "Ordinary days, huh. {i}(laughing softly){/i} Even though no day is really ordinary if you listen close enough. Okay. Let's go with that."

translate en b32_006:
    yara "Thanks, Kai. {i}(turning, half-jogging away){/i} Gotta run to the teachers' office first— oh, I'll let you know about something this afternoon. Wait for it!"

translate en b32r_001:
    "On the notice board near the counseling room, a fresh sheet of paper has been pinned up. Official letterhead, from a top arts university in Yogyakarta. A list of admitted applicants. On line thirteen, printed in bold: {b}Yara Kirana — Music (Sound Design).{/b}"

translate en b32r_002:
    kai_hati "She got in. Her portfolio got accepted. That tripod I hauled all over town… actually got her all the way there."

translate en b32r_003:
    "Yara sees her name on the sheet and doesn't scream. She just freezes for a moment — then a wide, completely genuine smile breaks across her face. Her first move isn't to the teachers' office. She takes off running down the hall."

translate en b32r_004:
    kai_hati "She's looking for me. I know she's looking for me."

translate en b32r_005:
    yara "{i}(from down the hall, out of breath){/i} Kai!"

translate en b32r_006:
    "Kai glances back for a split second. Twenty meters away, Yara is sprinting toward him — face glowing, a sheet of paper clutched in a hand shaking with joy. Inside Kai's pants pocket, the red August 1st tape feels like hot metal."

translate en b32r_007:
    kai_hati "August first. The day she says goodbye in tears. {i}(swallowing hard){/i} If she's this happy today… because of me… how wrecked is she gonna be when we say goodbye? No. Can't do it. Pull away now. Right now, before it gets even—"

translate en b32r_008:
    "Before Yara can close the distance, Kai whips around. Long strides, breaking into a half-run — straight down the emergency stairs toward the empty back courtyard."

translate en b32r_009:
    yara "Kai! Wait!"

translate en b32r_010:
    "Yara runs faster, ignoring the confused stares from younger students in the hall. Kai is quicker, though. Around the bend of the lower corridor, that gray jacket disappears."

translate en b32r_011:
    "Yara reaches the bottom of the stairs. The hallway is empty. Just a cool breeze sweeping dry leaves across the courtyard paving stones. The acceptance sheet in her fist slowly crumples in her grip. The smile that just bloomed fades away, leaving a hollow confusion behind."

translate en b32r_012:
    yara "{i}(quietly, to the empty hallway){/i} Why, Kai? …Why is it that right when my world finally starts sounding beautiful, you choose to go deaf?"

translate en b32s_001:
    "On this road, the sheet on the notice board is the same: {b}Yara Kirana — Music (Sound Design), Yogyakarta.{/b} Accepted. And just as it should be, Yara's first move isn't to the teachers' office — she runs down the hallway looking for Kai. Only one difference: on this road, Kai doesn't run."

translate en b32s_002:
    yara "{i}(running up, breathless, holding the paper high){/i} Kai! Kai, look— I got in! Yogya! Sound Design! I actually got in!"

translate en b32s_003:
    kai_hati "Yogya. So far away. She's really going. {i}(pause){/i} My chest tightens immediately — yet she's standing right in front of me, beaming like this, and she ran to me first. Not the teachers' office. To me."

translate en b32s_004a:
    kai "Yar… congrats. Seriously, huge congrats. {i}(smiling, then softer){/i} I'd be lying if I said I'm only happy. I'm scared. You're going far away, I'm staying here… I'm scared we'll turn into strangers. That's my problem to deal with, though. Today's your day. Congrats, Yar."

translate en b32s_005a:
    yara "{i}(pausing for a beat, her smile turning gentler){/i} …Thanks for being honest. Most people just say \"congrats\" and leave it at that. {i}(patting Kai's arm){/i} We'll talk about the distance later. Slowly. Right now… buy me a strawberry milk. To celebrate."

translate en b32s_004b:
    kai "Oh— Yogya? Wow. Good for you. Congrats."

translate en b32s_005b:
    yara "{i}(her smile dipping slightly){/i} …Just \"good for you\"? {i}(a small, forced laugh){/i} Alright then. Thanks. I… I'll go report to the teachers' office first."

translate en b32s_006b:
    kai_hati "There were a thousand sentences in my head just now. Only three words came out. And her face dropped right away. I saw it. I saw it, and I still kept my mouth shut."

translate en b32s_004c:
    kai "{i}(barely glancing at the paper){/i} Oh. Congrats. {i}(checking his watch){/i} I've got stuff to do in class, Yar. Catch up later, okay?"

translate en b32s_005c:
    yara "{i}(stopping short, the paper slowly lowering in her hand){/i} …Stuff to do? {i}(pause){/i} Okay. Okay, Kai. Go ahead."

translate en b32s_006c:
    kai_hati "\"Stuff to do.\" What stuff? Nothing. I just… couldn't stand seeing her that happy about something that's going to take her away from here. So I walked away first. Easier that way."

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 33 — Tangled Threads [RED ROUTE]
################################################################################

translate en b33_001:
    "Kai can't sleep a wink that night. The room that used to be his hiding place feels like an interrogation cell. Every time he shuts his eyes, he sees Yara's face by the stairwell — a face that deserved to celebrate her dream, wilting instead because of how cold he'd been."

translate en b33_002:
    kai_hati "I'm wrecking the present… just to brace for one minute of tears on August first. One minute. That isn't even— {i}(pressing a hand to his hollow chest){/i} \"Protecting.\" Protecting who? The only thing I'm protecting is my own fear."

translate en b33_003:
    kai "{i}(whispering into the dark){/i} I have to fix this."

translate en b33_004:
    "The next day, Kai waits in front of the Class XI-Social lockers. In his hand: a bottle of strawberry milk, Yara's favorite. Yara walks up with her black headphones clamped tight around her neck. Kai steps forward, stiff."

translate en b33_005:
    kai "Yara. {i}(trying to smile){/i} Congrats on… passing selection. Your new university. Here— {i}(holding out the bottle){/i} for you."

translate en b33_006:
    yara "{i}(looking at the bottle, then at Kai's face; there's no anger in her eyes — just exhaustion){/i} Thanks, Kai. I'm not really in the mood for milk right now."

translate en b33_007a:
    yara "{i}(before turning away, quietly){/i} That recording of your heartbeat… I listened to it last night. Sounded like someone running away from something. {i}(pause){/i} Guess you really were running, huh."

translate en b33_007b:
    yara "{i}(before turning away, quietly){/i} That shop wall clock… you recorded it for me, right? It ticks slower than I expected. {i}(pause){/i} Nothing like you lately. You're always in a rush. Who knows where to."

translate en b33_008:
    kai "{i}(fast, panicking){/i} Yara, about yesterday— I was just mixed up, I— listen to me first. Let's go to the flea market this afternoon, okay? I'll carry all your gear, every bit of it. I want to hear that old blacksmith's hammer. With you."

translate en b33_009:
    yara "{i}(letting out a short sigh; a razor-thin, bitter smile){/i} That blacksmith stopped hammering two days ago, Kai. And I already recorded it myself, the day before yesterday. Alone."

translate en b33_010:
    "Yara walks right past Kai without looking back. Kai stands frozen as the bottle of strawberry milk slowly goes cold in his hand."

translate en b33_011:
    kai_hati "Every word I said today came out off-key. Every time I try to get close, I just sound like a nuisance."

translate en b33_012:
    "That evening, Kai gets home with a pounding headache. The second he steps into his room, his desk greets him with an impossible sight: the future cassettes he'd shoved into his drawer — dusty and ignored for ages — have spilled out of their plastic shells. Dark brown tape ribbon coils out of them. Unnaturally."

translate en b33_013:
    "Beneath the desk lamp, the ribbons start spooling on their own. Slowly. Tangling. Twisting around each other across the teak desk — weaving a ruined black web, like threads of fate that lost their pattern. Inside its case, the red August 1st tape shudders violently. Its metal ribbon pulls taut, ready to snap."

translate en b33_014:
    kai "{i}(drops to the floor, breathing hard){/i} …"

translate en b33_015:
    kai_hati "I tried to control the future. I destroyed my own present to do it. And now… my fate has lost its melody. All that's left is noise. Noise ruining everything."

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 34 — Lifeless Music / The Intact Mixtape
################################################################################

translate en b34r_001:
    "His bedroom feels like a graveyard for sound. The mess of tangled tape ribbons still lies scattered across the desk like dead cobwebs. With shaking hands, Kai reaches into his bottom drawer."

translate en b34r_001_p2:
    "Out comes his beat-up silver Walkman. Already loaded inside is a red plastic cassette — the mixtape the two of them made together under the rain-splashed porch of Pak Ageng's shop. Voice messages to their past selves."

translate en b34r_002:
    "Earphones in. His cold thumb hits play."

translate en b34r_003:
    yara_kaset "To the Yara from a month ago, standing alone at the bus stop clamping her hands over her ears because she hated how loud the world was… Don't be scared of all the noisy sounds around you…"

translate en b34r_004:
    "Kai squeezes his eyes shut. He waits for the warmth that always used to spread through his chest whenever he heard Yara's voice. Waits for the flutter. The longing. Or even an ache — anything to prove he still has a soul."

translate en b34r_005:
    "Nothing. Yara's voice is crisp, lovely — and completely flat. Like a random song playing on a mall radio. Pretty, yet nothing to do with him."

translate en b34r_006b:
    kai_kaset "To the Kai locking himself in his room writing ridiculous goodbye letters… Put the pen down. You're not going to die this Friday. In fact, you're about to really start living after that dark broth and the sound of the train tracks…"

translate en b34r_007b:
    kai_hati "\"That dark broth and the sound of the train tracks.\" I know that's supposed to mean an important afternoon. I know — logically I know — we sat and ate rawon by the tracks together."

translate en b34r_008b:
    kai_hati "I just can't picture it. Can't remember the warmth of the rawon broth in that pouring rain. Can't remember her laughing over spicy chili right next to me. Blank. Like somebody tore a page straight out of the middle of the book."

translate en b34r_006c:
    kai_kaset "To the Kai locking himself in his room writing ridiculous goodbye letters… Put the pen down. You're not going to die this Friday. In fact, you're about to really start living after that first gust of wind up on Bukit Banyak…"

translate en b34r_007c:
    kai_hati "\"That first gust of wind up on Bukit Banyak.\" I know that place. I know — logically I know — we hiked up there hauling a tripod."

translate en b34r_008c:
    kai_hati "I just can't picture it. Can't remember sitting beside her on that hilltop. Can't remember her little yelp or the relief in my chest that day. Blank. Like somebody tore a page straight out of the middle of the book."

translate en b34r_006a:
    kai_kaset "To the Kai locking himself in his room writing ridiculous goodbye letters… Put the pen down. You're not going to die this Friday. In fact, you're about to really start living after that stack of books comes crashing down…"

translate en b34r_007a:
    kai_hati "\"That stack of books comes crashing down.\" I know that's supposed to mean something huge. I know — logically I know — that's how I met Yara."

translate en b34r_008a:
    kai_hati "I just can't picture it. Can't remember the sunset light in the library that day. Can't remember the panic on her face when she dropped those books. Blank. Like somebody tore a page straight out of the middle of the book."

translate en b34r_009:
    "Kai pulls the earphones out slowly. Tears roll down his cheeks — yet he can't even feel proper sadness. All that's left is emptiness. Cold. Terrifying."

translate en b34r_010:
    kai_hati "So this is what happens when you give away the start of a story. None of the chapters after… ever sound the same again."

translate en b34s_001:
    "On this road, Kai's bottom drawer holds the exact same silver Walkman and the exact same red plastic cassette — the mixtape from Pak Ageng's porch, made under the blowing rain. Only difference: no tangled ribbons on the desk. And Kai's memories are intact."

translate en b34s_002:
    yara_kaset "To the Yara from a month ago, standing alone at the bus stop clamping her hands over her ears because she hated how loud the world was… Don't be scared of all the noisy sounds around you…"

translate en b34s_003:
    kai_kaset "To the Kai locking himself in his room writing ridiculous goodbye letters… Put the pen down. You're not going to die this Friday. In fact, you're about to really start living after that stack of books comes crashing down…"

translate en b34s_004:
    kai_hati "That stack of books. {i}(smiling softly, alone in his room){/i} I remember. Sunset light in the library. Her panicking, books tumbling everywhere, and me — instead of walking away — bending down to help pick them up. Such a weird day. The day… everything started."

translate en b34s_005:
    "The warmth he was waiting for actually comes. Yara's voice on the tape isn't some stranger's song on a mall radio. It's his Yara. The laugh he knows by heart. The girl heading off to Yogya — and for the first time, that thought feels sad in a normal way. Not hollow. Sadness with something real inside it."

translate en b34s_006:
    kai_hati "I used to think those future tapes were what kept me calm. Turns out they weren't. {i}(looking at the red plastic cassette){/i} This one doesn't tell the future at all. It's only the past. And weirdly… this is the one that calms me down."

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 35 — Dust in the Dry Alley
################################################################################

translate en b35_001:
    "At noon, flyers for the student showcase go up on the notice board and get passed around classrooms. On the student portfolio list, one title sits in official print:"

translate en b35_002a:
    "\"Honest Sounds\" · by Yara Kirana."

translate en b35_002b:
    "\"Small Town, Big Sounds\" · by Yara Kirana."

translate en b35_002c:
    "\"Archive of Ordinary Days\" · by Yara Kirana."

translate en b35_003:
    kai_hati "That title… I picked that. {i}(pause){/i} It's small, sure. Still, my name — well, my choice — ended up printed along her path. Feels weird. Happy, with a little ache mixed in."

translate en b35_004:
    "That afternoon, something's off. The alley leading to Gema Masa — always damp, always smelling like rain-soaked earth — is dry today. Bone dry. The afternoon sun blazes in a cloudless sky. The cement ground is webbed with fine cracks, dust kicking up every time a hot breeze blows through. It's the first time Kai has ever seen the alley like this."

translate en b35_005:
    kai_hati "…Why's it dry? This alley is never dry. {i}(picking up his pace){/i} Pak Ageng…"

translate en b35_006a:
    "Click. Dry alley, drifting dust, the old shop at the end. A photo that feels wrong — like taking a picture of someone you know without their smile."

translate en b35_006b:
    "He switches on his phone's recorder. Crunch… crunch… Footsteps over dusty concrete. No splash of water. No dripping eaves. Just dry."

translate en b35_006c:
    "No time to stop for the alley. A sinking feeling drowns out his curiosity, and Kai's legs break into a run."

translate en b35_007:
    "Kai reaches the shop half-running, the tips of his shoes coated in dust. His stomach drops. Gema Masa's wooden door is shut tight. A heavy iron padlock — already rusted — locks it from the outside. The little sign that usually says \"Open\" has been flipped around. On the back, in dull red ink: {b}CLOSED{/b}."

translate en b35_008:
    kai "Pak Ageng… {i}(pounding on the door with a shaking palm){/i} Pak Ageng! It's me, Kai! Please open the door, Pak!"

translate en b35_009:
    "No answer. The silence inside feels thick and dead — nothing like the warm hush that usually wraps around that cassette-lined room. Kai presses his ear to the crack in the door. No creaking rocking chair. No slow footsteps. Nothing at all."

translate en b35_010:
    "Then comes a sound: a cough. Dry, heavy, from the side window connected to Pak Ageng's living quarters behind the shop. Terribly weak. Every breath sounds like a fight."

translate en b35_011:
    kai "{i}(rushing to the window, tapping the glass in panic){/i} Pak Ageng? Are you sick? Pak, please open the window!"

translate en b35_012:
    "The curtain shifts slightly. Through the dusty glass, the dim room inside barely comes into view: Pak Ageng lying frail on his old bed, wrapped in a thick sarung. His face is deathly pale. His eyes — usually calm and sharp — look dim, worn out."

translate en b35_013:
    "Pak Ageng turns his head slowly toward the window. He sees Kai panicking outside. All he does is shake his head — barely moving. His trembling hand lifts, pointing toward the padlock on the shop door. Then his fingers wave gently, gesturing: go. This shop can't help you today."

translate en b35_014:
    kai "{i}(steps back; his hands drop limp at his sides){/i} …"

translate en b35_015:
    kai_hati "My safe place… just collapsed. Pak Ageng is sick in bed, helpless, and the shop is shut. I'm all alone out here. Trapped between a past that's already been erased… and a future chasing me down with zero mercy."
